# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.vscode/
.idea/

# scratch
tmp/
_CLAUDE-INBOX/

# Claude Code local machine settings (per-machine, not shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Secrets. site/.env is deliberately tracked because it holds only DOMAIN and
# ACME_EMAIL, which are public facts the deploy needs. NEVER put an API key,
# token, or password in it. Anything genuinely secret goes in one of these
# instead, which are ignored:
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.production
.env.secrets
secrets/
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# Content mirror: text only. The image and PDF masters stay on disk because they
# are ~1.74 GB and git is the wrong place for them. If they ever need to be
# versioned, use Git LFS rather than committing them here.
content/**/*.png
content/**/*.jpg
content/**/*.jpeg
content/**/*.pdf
content/**/*.woff2
content/**/*.docx
content/**/*.xlsx
content/**/*.zip

# generated preview, regenerate with python ops/send_brief.py --preview
ops/brief-preview.html

# Every ops/tests/*.py scratch page (audit_visual.py's own probe,
# test_audit_catalog.py, test_audit_links.py, test_gates.py,
# test_measure_events.py, test_mobile_overflow.py, test_quest_flow.py,
# test_web_to_mobile_import.py) writes its fixture under an underscore-
# prefixed name for exactly this reason and cleans up only in a finally
# block or a context manager's __exit__, which a SIGTERM from an outer
# timeout can skip. No real page anywhere in site/ starts with an
# underscore, so this ignores the whole convention at once instead of one
# literal filename per script. gate_no_stray_probe_files in preflight.py
# fails loudly if one is ever found sitting in the tree regardless.
site/**/_*.html

# Python bytecode. Tracking it means every run of any script shows up
# as a repository change, and a stale .pyc can shadow a source edit.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
ops/last-brief.json

# Generated product files. 155 of them, rebuilt by ops/build_catalog.py from
# content.json in seconds. Committing 3 MB of derived HTML would bloat every
# clone for no benefit; the generator is the source of truth.
build/products/
build/heroes/
build/deck-review/
build/cards-rendered/
# Print-ready bleed sheets, 178 PNGs at 826x1126, rebuilt by
# ops/build_card_template.py --bleed and ops/render_cards.py --bleed.
build/cards-rendered-bleed/
build/card-fronts-bleed/
build/cardtext/
build/card-fronts/
build/video/test/
build/video/_frames/
build/models/
build/generated/
build/shots/

# Intermediate render scratch: per-beat TTS mp3s and PNG frames.
# These were tracked, so the narration batch dirtied the working tree
# continuously and every rebase failed with 'cannot rebase: you have
# unstaged changes'. A push that fails whenever a render is running is
# not a push that works every time.
build/video/_narr/

# Rendered video is a build artifact, not source. 794 files and 785 MB of it
# were tracked, .git reached 1,087 MB, and every clone dragged the whole
# history for files that ops/render_all_narrated.py regenerates from the zone
# data in this repository.
#
# Phil's decision, 2026-09-03: keep video out of git going forward. The
# deliverable lives in Desktop/6s-success-videos, which is where it is
# actually used from, and on YouTube once published.
#
# Captions and the per-video YouTube metadata stay tracked deliberately: they
# are small, they are edited by hand, and losing them would mean rewriting
# copy rather than re-running a renderer.
build/video/zones/*.mp4
build/video/zones-16x9/*.mp4
build/video/zones-narrated/*.mp4
build/video/zones-photo/*.mp4
build/video/cards/*.mp4
build/video/test/
build/video/*.log
build/video/*.log.err
build/video/frames/
